@startuml fig2_resources
' Diagram 2 of the AIAS alignment: the resources of a plant.
'
' Conventions: shared/FIGURES.md, with prefixes for the reason diagram 1 gives.
'
' What it shows: the device classes a model of a plant uses, and the two
' bridges a resource has into other subdomains.
'
' All seven device classes come from no standard. They are constructs of this
' work, and ALIGNMENT.md records them apart from the bridges that do rest on
' one. Relating them to a classification of equipment such as ECLASS is open
' work, and the note in the drawing says so.
'
' Left out on purpose: the three main classes, which diagram 1 shows, and the
' relations of the function level, which diagram 3 shows.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 22
skinparam ranksep 42
skinparam padding 3
skinparam ArrowColor #1A2733
skinparam ArrowFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontColor #1A2733
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF8E1
skinparam NoteBorderColor #C9A227
skinparam NoteFontSize 12
hide empty members
hide circle
skinparam class {
  BackgroundColor #FCEFC7
  BorderColor #C9A227
  FontColor #1A2733
  FontSize 13
  BorderThickness 1
}

class "aias:Component" as Component
class "aias:Resource"  as Resource
class "aias:Product"   as Product

Component <|-- Resource
Component <|-- Product

class "aias:Sensor"        as Sensor
class "aias:Actuator"      as Actuator
class "aias:Controller"    as Controller
class "aias:EdgeDevice"    as EdgeDevice
class "aias:Computer"      as Computer
class "aias:InternalCloud" as InternalCloud
class "aias:ExternalCloud" as ExternalCloud

Resource <|-- Sensor
Resource <|-- Actuator
Resource <|-- Controller
Resource <|-- EdgeDevice
Resource <|-- Computer
Resource <|-- InternalCloud
Resource <|-- ExternalCloud

note bottom of Actuator
  Means the element acting on the flow.
  IEC 60050-351 uses actuator, 351-49-07,
  for the signal side driving it, so the
  two are deliberately not related.
end note

' ===================================================================
'  Where a resource reaches into other subdomains
' ===================================================================

class "vdi3682:TechnicalResource" as TechnicalResource
class "iso7498:OpenSystem"        as OpenSystem
class "iec60050:PhysicalUnit"     as PhysicalUnit

Resource -up- TechnicalResource : owl:equivalentClass
Component -up-> "*" OpenSystem : aias:appearsAsOpenSystem
Resource -up-|> PhysicalUnit

TechnicalResource -[hidden]right- PhysicalUnit
PhysicalUnit      -[hidden]right- OpenSystem

note right of PhysicalUnit
  A subclass, not an equivalence. Every
  resource is a physical unit, but not
  every physical unit performs a
  transformation, so an equivalence would
  be wrong in one direction.
end note

' Layout only. The device fan is left to the renderer: Resource carries four
' edges upwards, and forcing rows against them pushes Component out of place.

@enduml
